# On the Dynamics of Quality Student Enrollment at Institutions of Higher Education.

**Authors:** Mayer-Foulkes, David

## Abstract
Develops an inter-temporal optimization model linking academic achievement reputation, and the pool of student quality available to an institution. Describes empirical study of student-quality dynamics and its relation to the model. Finds that SAT levels of attracted students follow a convergent process as predicted, with graduation rates, expenditure, and reputation combining to attract better future students. (Contains 12 references.) (Author/PKP)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ652058

